{\rtf1\ansi\deff0\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fs28\b\cf1 SAP S/4HANA Order-to-Cash (O2C) Functional Design\cf0\b0\par\par\fs20\b Document Type:\b0 Functional Design Document\par\b Version:\b0 1.0\par\b Prepared By:\b0 Business & IT Design Team\par\b Date:\b0 2026-10-08\par\b Confidentiality:\b0 Internal / Client Confidential\par\par\pard\fs24\b 1. Executive Summary\b0\par\fs20 This functional design document defines the end-to-end Order-to-Cash (O2C) process for SAP S/4HANA. The O2C lifecycle starts with customer inquiry and ends with cash realization. The design supports sales, logistics, billing, credit management, and finance functions in a unified SAP environment and provides process controls, automation opportunities, and KPI visibility.\par\par\pard\fs24\b 2. Business Objective\b0\par\fs20 The objective of this design is to enable a consistent, efficient, and auditable O2C process that improves customer experience, reduces order cycle time, enhances billing accuracy, supports credit risk management, and strengthens receivables performance.\par\par\pard\fs24\b 3. Scope\b0\par\fs20\b In Scope:\b0\par - Customer master data management\par - Sales inquiry and quotation\par - Sales order creation and maintenance\par - Pricing and tax validation\par - Availability check and order confirmation\par - Delivery and goods issue processing\par - Billing and invoice creation\par - Accounts receivable and cash application\par - Credit management and dispute handling\par - Returns, credits, and claim management\par - Reporting and KPI monitoring\par\par\b Out of Scope:\b0\par - Vendor management and procurement\par - HR and payroll processes\par - Non-O2C products outside the sales lifecycle\par\par\pard\fs24\b 4. Business Context\b0\par\fs20 The company operates a B2B sales model across multiple channels, including direct sales, distributors, and partner networks. The existing O2C process suffers from manual intervention, delayed billing, inconsistent credit controls, and poor visibility into order and invoice status. The SAP S/4HANA target design addresses these pain points by standardizing process flow, automating validation checks, and enabling better operational monitoring.\par\par\pard\fs24\b 5. Process Overview\b0\par\fs20\par\fs18\b Customer Inquiry\b0\par\tab -> \b Quotation\b0\par\tab -> \b Sales Order Creation\b0\par\tab -> \b Pricing and Tax Check\b0\par\tab -> \b Availability Check\b0\par\tab -> \b Delivery Creation\b0\par\tab -> \b Goods Issue\b0\par\tab -> \b Billing\b0\par\tab -> \b AR Posting\b0\par\tab -> \b Payment Receipt / Cash Application\b0\par\tab -> \b Collections and Closure\b0\par\par\fs20\b Visual Process Flow:\b0\par\par\pard\fs18\f0\fs18 [Customer Inquiry] -> [Quotation] -> [Sales Order] -> [Availability Check] -> [Delivery] -> [Goods Issue] -> [Billing] -> [AR Posting] -> [Payment Receipt] -> [Collections / Close]\par\par\pard\fs24\b 6. Detailed Functional Process\b0\par\fs20\b 6.1 Customer Master Data\b0\par - Maintain customer master with sold-to, ship-to, bill-to, and payer relationship\par - Validate customer legal names, addresses, tax IDs, and payment terms\par - Maintain credit control area, payment method, and sales area assignments\par - Manage account group and partner function configuration\par\par\b 6.2 Inquiry and Quotation\b0\par - Create inquiry or quotation based on customer request\par - Maintain valid price conditions, freight, discount, and taxes\par - Route approval for discounts above threshold\par - Store product and service assumptions in customer-facing documents\par\par\b 6.3 Sales Order Creation\b0\par - Create standard sales orders in SAP S/4HANA\par - Validate material, plant, quantity, and availability\par - Maintain schedule lines and delivery dates\par - Support order amendments, partial deliveries, and cancellations\par\par\b 6.4 Pricing and Tax Validation\b0\par - Determine pricing using condition records and pricing procedure\par - Validate freight and discounts according to policy\par - Apply relevant tax determination based on customer and destination\par - Prevent billing when pricing data is incomplete or inconsistent\par\par\b 6.5 Availability Check and Confirmation\b0\par - Run ATP checks for inventory and upcoming receipts\par - Confirm or partially confirm orders\par - Raise shortages and backorder exceptions\par - Trigger material or route escalation when required\par\par\b 6.6 Delivery and Warehouse Processing\b0\par - Create outbound deliveries from confirmed orders\par - Support partial deliveries and route-based dispatch\par - Coordinate with warehouse for packing and staging\par - Post goods issue only after validation and stock confirmation\par\par\b 6.7 Billing and Invoice Posting\b0\par - Generate billing documents from delivery or service confirmation\par - Validate pricing, tax, payment terms, and legal entity\par - Support invoice split, debit memo, and credit memo scenarios\par - Trigger invoice output to customer through print or electronic format\par\par\b 6.8 Accounts Receivable and Payment\b0\par - Post receivables on billing document creation\par - Track open items and aging\par - Apply incoming customer payments to outstanding invoice items\par - Manage residual, partial, or unapplied cash through exception workflow\par\par\b 6.9 Credit Management\b0\par - Assess customer exposure and limit utilization\par - Block or release orders based on credit rules\par - Escalate high-risk accounts to credit review\par - Supports approval flow for exceptions and overrides\par\par\b 6.10 Returns and Claims\b0\par - Process return orders and return deliveries\par - Capture return reason codes and damage conditions\par - Create credit memo or refund with defined approval matrix\par - Track dispute resolution and aging\par\par\pard\fs24\b 7. Master Data Requirements\b0\par\fs20 - Customer master\par - Material master\par - Condition records and pricing procedure\par - Tax determination rules\par - Output determination settings\par - Payment terms and credit control area\par - Ship-to, bill-to, payer relationships\par - Sales organization, distribution channel, division\par - Plant and shipping point data\par\par\pard\fs24\b 8. Functional Requirements by Role\b0\par\fs20\b Sales User\b0\par - Create and maintain sales orders\par - Validate pricing and delivery dates\par - Monitor order status and fulfillment\par\par\b Warehouse/Logistics User\b0\par - Confirm deliveries\par - Post goods issue\par - Manage stock and dispatch exceptions\par\par\b Billing User\b0\par - Create and review invoices\par - Resolve billing errors and reversals\par - Trigger invoice communication\par\par\b Finance / AR User\b0\par - Review open items and aging\par - Post incoming customer payments\par - Support dispute and cash application workflows\par\par\b Credit Manager\b0\par - Review credit exposure\par - Approve or reject blocked orders\par - Maintain override and review procedures\par\par\pard\fs24\b 9. Business Rules and Controls\b0\par\fs20 - Orders cannot be created for blocked customers without approval\par - Material and account validations are mandatory\par - Prices must match approved condition records\par - Tax is determined according to legal and customer location\par - Billing may only occur after valid delivery or service confirmation\par - Payment terms must align with commercial agreement\par - Reversals and manual adjustments require proper authorization\par - Returns and credits require documented reason code\par - Financial postings must be traceable to source documents\par\par\pard\fs24\b 10. Integration Points\b0\par\fs20 The O2C scenario integrates with:\par - Master data management\par - Warehouse and inventory management\par - Finance and accounts receivable\par - Tax and compliance systems\par - External customer portals or EDI channels\par - Payment processing and bank integration\par - Analytics and executive reporting\par\par\pard\fs24\b 11. Exceptions and Issue Handling\b0\par\fs20 Common exceptions include:\par - Credit block\par - Material shortage\par - Pricing inconsistency\par - Delivery failure\par - Goods issue posting error\par - Billing rejection\par - Payment mismatch\par - Customer dispute or invoice query\par - Return authorization failure\par\par Standard handling approach:\par - Assign exception owner\par - Set resolution SLA\par - Record root cause and corrective action\par - Monitor recurring issues via governance meetings\par\par\pard\fs24\b 12. Key Performance Indicators\b0\par\fs20 - Order fulfillment cycle time\par - On-time delivery rate\par - Invoice accuracy rate\par - Days Sales Outstanding (DSO)\par - Collection efficiency\par - Credit exposure utilization\par - Billing dispute rate\par - Returns and credit memo rate\par\par\pard\fs24\b 13. Security and Authorization\b0\par\fs20 Role-based access should be implemented for order creation, delivery processing, billing, payment posting, and credit review. Users must be restricted to the sales area, company code, and business function relevant to their role.\par\par\pard\fs24\b 14. SDLC Alignment\b0\par\fs20\b Requirements Phase:\b0 Capture business requirements, KPI targets, and process scope\par\b Design Phase:\b0 Configure master data, process flow, controls, approvals, and interfaces\par\b Build Phase:\b0 Configure SAP transactions and business logic\par\b Test Phase:\b0 Execute unit, integration, UAT, and regression testing\par\b Deployment Phase:\b0 Conduct cutover, go-live, and hypercare support\par\b Support Phase:\b0 Maintain process governance and continuous improvement\par\par\pard\fs24\b 15. Risks and Mitigation\b0\par\fs20 - Poor master data quality -> data cleansing and validation\par - Delayed collections -> credit and receivables governance\par - Tax and invoice errors -> automated validation and reconciliation\par - Process bottlenecks -> KPI monitoring and workflow redesign\par - User resistance -> role-based training and readiness activities\par\par\pard\fs24\b 16. Acceptance Criteria\b0\par\fs20 - End-to-end O2C flow is mapped and approved\par - Master data and pricing rules are standardized\par - Credit and payment controls are defined\par - Integrations and exception handling are tested\par - Reporting and KPI metrics are approved\par - User roles and authorization are validated\par\par\pard\fs24\b 17. Approval\b0\par\fs20 Business Process Owner\par Finance Lead\par Sales Operations Lead\par IT Solution Architect\par SAP Functional Lead\par Security & Controls Lead\par\par\pard\fs24\b 18. Conclusion\b0\par\fs20 The SAP S/4HANA Order-to-Cash process is a strategic business cycle that directly affects revenue, cash flow, and customer service quality. This functional design establishes a clear, scalable, and controlled process foundation that supports both operational execution and enterprise reporting.\par\par\fs20\b End of Document\b0\par}